  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed replacement of the subdivided house's specified existing front, side and rear single glazed windows, and ground floor side and rear doors, with matching designed, slimline double glazed windows and doors, without the submission of a detailed condition survey assessing each relevant existing window and door and justifying its replacement as the only feasible approach and accurate, detailed existing and proposed technical elevations/ sections for each replacement and door to enable assessment of the proposal's design accuracy, would result in excessive loss of historic fabric from and poor quality, historically inaccurate alterations to the Grade II listed subdivided house that which would not be outweighed by the proposal's limited public benefit of marginally improving the building's energy efficiency and reducing its climate change impact and harm the significance and character of the Grade II listed building and Bedford Park Conservation Area, contrary to Policies HE5 and HE6 of the National Planning Policy Framework, London Plan Policies D4 and HC1 and Local Plan Policies SC7, CC1, CC2 and CC4 and the Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD: Residential Extension Guidelines.  "
